      "title": "Career Development",
      "description": "Career Development | Keuka College Skip to main content Request More Info Apply Now Text a Question 1-800-335-3852 Search Menu Academics Majors and Programs Online & Graduate Field Period Experiential Learning Career Development Global Education Records and Registration Library Academic Success Center HEOP Honors Program Online Bookstore Admissions Freshman Admissions Transfer Admissions International Admissions Graduate Admissions Online and Graduate Visit Campus Contact Us Honors Program Apply Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid Understanding Financial Aid Tuition & Scholarships Net Price Calculator Life at KC Housing & Dining Fun & Adventure Health & Counseling Campus Safety Keuka Lake Area Community & Belonging Student Employment Information Technology Campus Store Mail & Packages Athletics Field Period Blog KC Portal Email News Directory About Library Alumni Make a Gift Campus Store Help Search Popular Searches Academic Calendar Campus Store Library Moodle Nixle Parking Map Portal Office of Records and Registration Student Printing More at Keuka College Conference Services Diversity & Inclusion Human Resources Title IX Weddings Career Development Academics Academics Menu Academics Majors & Programs Experiential Learning Field Period® Career Development Global Education Records and Registration Lightner Library Academic Success Center Academic Advising Bookstore We're here to help you succeed after college Career development is dedicated to helping you succeed in your chosen career—even if you don't quite know what that is yet. We can help you choose a major and profession, develop your career path, find internships and full-time jobs, find and apply to graduate programs, network with alumni, and make a successful transition into your career. How do we help you succeed? Career Fairs Annual career fairs bring 65+ employers who are looking for you to campus. Graduate Fairs Grad fairs help you decide what to do and where to go next. Through the College's membership in the Rochester Area Career Development Association , students have access to fairs attracting 80+ schools and programs. KC Career Connections Our exclusive, online job board brings hundreds of job, internship, Field Period®, and volunteer opportunities to our students and alumni.​ Login Now Preparing for your Job Search When you're ready to start applying, we're here to look over your résumé and cover letters and practice your interviewing skills. We'll help you put your best foot forward! Networking We'll help you start your network early through connections with our alumni and employers. Career Planning Unsure of your major or career path? We provide personalized assistance and the option to take powerful career assessments such as the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator and the Strong Interest Inventory. You Might Also Like 5 Ways Keuka College Keeps Online Students Connected and Supported Study anywhere, on your schedule – while still feeling known, supported, and part of a community. Keuka College, Finger Lakes Health Partner to Strengthen Regional Healthcare Keuka College’s Occupational Therapy Program Earns Highest National Accreditation Status Keuka College Brings RN to BS in Nursing Program Back to Canandaigua Keuka College, Finger Lakes Community Health Partner to Strengthen Regional Healthcare Workforce Keuka College and Syracuse Create New Master’s Pathways for STEM Students Keuka College Launches First-Ever Full-Time Intensive Master of Science in Leadership Keuka College-Yates County Partnership Invests in the Region’s Future A Keuka College Ocean Scientist Found a New Way to Restore Coral Reefs Keuka College and W–FL BOCES Forge Shared Pathways to Higher Learning and Career Success Keuka College Students Find Connections Across Cultures in Panama Popular Searches Academic Calendar Campus Store Library Moodle Nixle Parking Map Portal Office of Records and Registration Student Printing Wellness Weekend at the Lake More at Keuka College Conferenc